WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.750
In 1776, Adam Smith
argued that self-interest,

2
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:08.000
in competitive markets,
could serve society,

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.310
led by an invisible hand.

4
00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.040
Less than a century later,

5
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:14.660
Karl Marx looked at the
industrial cities of his

6
00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.530
day and saw something very different.

7
00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:20.070
Both men studied market economies.

8
00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:23.440
Yet they gave very different
answers to one question:

9
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.580
what role should the state play?

10
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:27.980
Should governments leave markets alone?

11
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:31.790
And why have such brilliant minds
given such different answers?

12
00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:35.540
In this mission, you'll travel
a timeline of economic ideas,

13
00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.660
and see the problem each
thinker was trying to solve.

14
00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:41.240
Then you'll place each
thinker on a line running

15
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:44.100
from mostly market to mostly state.

16
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:49.080
Your mission: explain why great economists
answer this question so differently.
